  "source_ref": "Sundance EMC2-DP Design Specification (QCF51) Issue 3.3.0 section 8 'FMC Pin-Out' (carrier FMC J3 to SoM B2B routing; all 34 LA pairs, CLK0/CLK1, SCL/SDA verified on their VITA 57.1 LPC positions); FPGA package balls from first-party schematic-derived, Vivado-verified reference data for the EMC2-DP V2 + TE0820 build; banks from the AMD SFVC784 package file (ball map verified identical between XCZU2CG and XCZU5EV in SFVC784). Excluded: DP0_C2M/DP0_M2C and GBTCLK0_M2C (carrier routes them to the SoM's MGT B2B pins = PS-GTR, not PL pins); PRSNT_M2C_L (routed to B2B JB2.37, no FPGA ball documented); FMC JTAG and GA0/GA1 (not connected to the SoM per the pin-out table). 13 LA/CLK pairs are intentionally polarity-inverted on the module (FMC _P on the FPGA pad's N side within the same diff pair). LA32 is routed to two single-ended-only balls (no diff pair).",
